new_text:
{"text": "A mother gave birth to a newborn two weeks ago. She started seeing blood little by little on her body. However, as the days went by, she noticed that something like the stomach and blood were coming out. Sometimes the mother of the child is different. And she has a neck that is not good. And she knows that the mother of the child usually has small pains in her lower abdomen, and every time she sees these signs, her heart gets confused. She wondered if it was something among the common problems after childbirth or another problem. One day when she went to the hospital, and was talking to other mothers, she heard that they should not downplay any changes they see in their bodies. This made her seek a doctor to talk to them. My question is, what can cause such a thing after childbirth? Can pain in the lower abdomen be a sign of a disease? What are the signs that this new mother should be careful of after childbirth? What are the steps that the mother needs to take to prevent this disease?", "text_language": "English", "translated_text": "Mama wey born pikin two weeks ago begin dey see small-small blood dey come from her body. As days dey pass, e notice say wetin resemble meat or tissue and blood dey come out. Sometimes e dey feel somehow, and e neck no dey okay. E still dey get small-small pain for under belle, and anytime e see all these signs, e dey fear and confuse. E begin wonder wetin dey happen,whether na normal thing wey fit happen after woman born pikin or whether na another sickness.

One day, as e go hospital and dey talk with other nursing mothers, e hear say make nobody ignore any change wey dem notice for their body after childbirth. That one make am decide say e go see doctor make dem examine am.

My question be: Wetin fit cause this kind problem after woman don born? Pain for under belle fit be signs of sickness? Which danger signs wey new mama suppose watch out for after childbirth? And wetin be the steps wey new mama need to take to prevent this kind sickness?", "translated_text_language": "Pidgin", "audio_language": "Pidgin", "text_was_edited": false}

{"text": "A woman noticed that her husband coughs very strongly when they wake up in the morning while still on the bed. The cough starts suddenly and takes a long time before it stops. As time goes on, she also notices that her husband struggles to breathe properly. When he walks a little distance or climbs stairs, he stops to catch his breath and becomes tired very quickly. One day, after her husband spent a long time coughing and trying to regain his breath, the wife became worried. She started thinking that maybe there is a disease causing all these problems. The next day, she spoke with her husband to go to the hospital so that they can see a doctor and know exactly what is happening. The question is what can cause a cough to be this severe, with constant tiredness and difficulty breathing all the time when the cough occurs? Can this problem be related only to lung disease or heart disease? What are the things that can cause death or make a person struggle to breathe severely, to the point that the person needs urgent medical attention? What are the danger signs of breathing problems that the family should watch out for regarding cough and difficulty in breathing?", "text_language": "English", "translated_text": "One woman notice say anytime wey dem wake up for morning, her husband go begin cough well well. The cough dey start suddenly and e fit take long time before e go stop. As time dey go, she notice say her husband no fit breathe well again. Anytime wey e waka small distance or climb staircase, e go stop make e catch breath because e dey tire quick quick.

One day, after her husband don spend long time dey cough and dey struggle to catch breath, the woman come fear. E begin think say maybe one sickness dey cause all these problems. The next day, she talk to her husband make dem go hospital go see doctor so dat doctor go fit examine am and know wetin dey really happen.

The question be say, wetin fit make person dey cough like this, with constant tiredness and serious difficulty to breathe anytime the cough start? Na only lung sickness or heart sickness fit cause this kind problem? Which kind sickness fit make person struggle to breathe so much or even cause death if dem no get urgent treatment? Wetin be the danger signs of cough and breathing problem wey family members suppose watch out for, wey mean say the person need urgent medical attention?", "translated_text_language": "Pidgin", "audio_language": "Pidgin", "text_was_edited": false}

{"text": "A woman was brought to the hospital this morning because she was bleeding heavily, and this had caused her a great deal of distress. She was asked whether this had happened to her before, and she replied that it had happened about twice previously, during which she usually experienced pain and the bleeding would occur intermittently. She was then asked whether she might be having a miscarriage, but she said she did not know whether she was pregnant or whether she had become pregnant. She was asked when she last had her menstrual period, and she replied that it had not been very long, as she had her last menstrual period about one and a half months ago before this bleeding started again this morning. Please, what could cause a woman to bleed this heavily? What emergency steps can be taken? What treatments can be given to this woman to save her life and stop the bleeding? What medicines or injections that help stop bleeding can be given to her first? And what investigations can be carried out to determine the cause of such severe bleeding?", "text_language": "English", "translated_text": "One woman dem carry come hospital this morning because she dey bleed plenty, and the bleeding don make her weak well-well. Dem ask am whether this kind thing don happen before, and she talk say e don happen about two times before. Anytime e happen, she dey feel pain and the bleeding dey come and stop, then come start again.

Dem come ask am whether e fit be say belle dey comot, but she talk say she no know whether she get belle or not. Dem ask am when she last see her monthly period, and she talk say not too long, say na about one month and two weeks ago she last see her period before this heavy bleeding start again this morning.

Abeg, wetin fit make dis woman bleed this kind plenty? Wetin be the emergency things wey health workers suppose do immediately? Wetin be the treatment wey fit save her life and stop the bleeding? Which medicine or injection wey fit help control the bleeding fit be given first? And which tests or investigations fit be done to know the real cause of this serious bleeding?", "translated_text_language": "Pidgin", "audio_language": "Pidgin", "text_was_edited": false}

{"text": "A 30-year-old woman gave birth a few minutes ago. The delivery was said to be normal. However, since the baby was born, the baby has been having serious difficulty. The baby is not crying well and is not responding as a newborn should. After birth, the baby did not cry properly, and seems to have difficulty waking up. The body seems stiff or not moving properly as expected. The baby also cannot feed well and is struggling to breastfeed. The mother is worried because her previous children used to cry immediately after birth. What can cause this problem? What tests can be done on the baby, and what emergency steps should be taken? What can be done for this newborn baby?", "text_language": "English", "translated_text": "One woman wey dey 30 years old don born pikin few minutes wey don pass. Dem talk say di delivery go normal. But since Dem born di pikin, di pikin dey get serious problem. Di pikin no dey cry well and e no dey respond like new baby suppose respond. After birth, di pikin no cry well at all and e be like say e dey find am hard to wake up. Di pikin body fit dey stiff or e no dey move well as dem expect. Di pikin no fit suck breast well and e dey struggle to breastfeed.

Di mama dey worry because all her other pikin dem cry immediately after dem born dem.

Wetin fit cause dis kain problem? Which kind test dem fit do for di pikin? Wetin be di emergency steps wey health workers suppose take immediately? And which kind treatment dem fit give dis newborn pikin?", "translated_text_language": "Pidgin", "audio_language": "Pidgin", "text_was_edited": false}

{"text": "A mother noticed that for the past few days, her child had started coughing continuously. At first, she thought it was a cold affecting the child’s chest and that it would go away. However, the cough did not improve. Every night, the child wakes up suddenly because of the cough. Sometimes, the child struggles as if it is difficult to breathe properly. The mother would carry the child upright and could hear the chest working while the child was breathing. This makes it difficult for the child to sleep well at night. One day, after a night during which the child coughed severely and struggled to breathe properly, the mother decided to go to the hospital. She wanted to know what was causing the cough, what was causing the breathing difficulty, and how she could help the child. My question is: what could cause a child to cough severely and have difficulty breathing, especially at night? What danger signs should they watch out for when the child is coughing? What things should they avoid in order to prevent or reduce this cough?", "text_language": "English", "translated_text": "One woman notice say for the past few days, pikin don dey cough without stopping. At first, she think say na ordinary cold wey catch the pikin for chest and say e go clear by itself. But the cough no gree stop. Every night, the pikin dey wake up suddenly because of the cough. Sometimes, e go dey struggle like say e hard am to breathe well.The woman go carry the pikin upright, and she fit hear the chest dey make sound and dey work hard as the pikin dey breathe. Because of this, the pikin no fit sleep well for night.

One day, after one night wey the pikin cough well-well and dey struggle to breathe properly, the woman decide say she must carry the pikin go hospital. She want know wetin dey cause the cough, wetin dey make the pikin find am hard to breathe, and how she fit help the pikin.

My question be: wetin fit make pikin cough seriously and find am hard to breathe, especially for night? Which kind danger signs dem suppose watch out for when pikin dey cough? Which things dem suppose avoid to help prevent or reduce this cough?", "translated_text_language": "Pidgin", "audio_language": "Pidgin", "text_was_edited": false}

{"text": "​A pregnant woman who is six months pregnant and lives in our house started noticing that her heart palpitates rapidly as if she just finished running. Sometimes she gets tired without doing any work at all, and her hands tremble slightly. After a few weeks, she also noticed that her neck started swelling in the front. When people began telling her that her neck looks different from before, she became very frightened, wondering if this is one of the illnesses that affect pregnant women or if it is another problem. She has now decided to go see a doctor so they can know what is causing it. My question is, what can cause a pregnant woman's heart to palpitate rapidly like someone who just finished running, along with her neck swelling? Can this problem affect the development of the baby inside her? What are the warning signs they should watch out for at home? Are there certain foods or drinks that she ought to avoid, or those that she should eat more of during this kind of period?", "text_language": "English", "translated_text": "One woman wey get belle for six months we dey stay our house begin notice say hin heart dey beat fast fast like person wey just finish race. Sometimes e go just just Dey tire even though e never do any work and hin hand dey shake small small. 
After some weeks, e come notice say front of hin neck begin swell. As people begin tell am say hin neck no be like before again, fear catch am. E begin wonder whether Na one of the sickness wey dey affect women wey get belle or whether Na another problem entirely.

Now e don decide say e wan go see doctor make dem check wetin dey cause am. My question be say wetin fit make pregnant woman heart dey beat fast like person wey just run finish, with neck swelling? This problem fit affect the growth and development of the pikin wey dey hin belle? Wetin be the danger signs wey dey suppose watch out for while dem dey house? And e get any type of food and drink wey dem suppose avoid, or any wey e suppose chop and drink during this kind time?", "translated_text_language": "Pidgin", "audio_language": "Pidgin", "text_was_edited": false}

{"text": "Good evening I came because of my younger sibling. I noticed that their eyes and skin have an airy... a pale/yellowish color. And this has been going on for about three days now. Their body is also very hot, burning with a fever, and they cannot eat. They cannot retain anything, they cannot retain anything. In fact, they are shivering/weakened heavily. Because their head is throbbing, their head is aching, and their body is burning hot. We have tried using some things at home, we gave them, but even so, there is absolutely no difference in their condition. Their eyes and skin that have that pale/yellowish color, it hasn't stopped, that yellow color is just increasing day by day, and they are not at peace, they are not comfortable, they are suffering, God forbid, they are really suffering. That is why I came to the hospital so we can know what to do, the steps we need to take, so that my younger sibling's body, their skin and eyes that are turning yellow, will stop, and they will recover.", "text_language": "English", "translated_text": "Good evening. I come because of my younger sibling. I notice say hin eye and skin don begin turn yellow. This thing don dey happen for three days now. Hin body too dey very hot, fever dey worry am, and e no fit chop anything. Anything wey hin chop no dey stay hin belle. E dey vomit everything. As if that one no reach, e dey shake well well because hin head dey pain am and hin whole body dey burn with fever. 

We don try give am some medicine for house, but nothing don change. That yellow color for hin eye and skin no gree stop, instead e dey increase everyday. E no dey comfortable at all, e dey really suffer. God forbid, e dey suffer too much. Na why I come hospital make una help us know wetin dey happen and wetin we suppose do. So that my younger sibling go recover and the yellow color for hin skin and eye disappear 
", "translated_text_language": "Pidgin", "audio_language": "Pidgin", "text_was_edited": false}
